ghee (0.3.0) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Panel drivers drop Adafruit-Blinka for spidev, libgpiod and smbus2, all
    of them in Debian main, so the deb can recommend them.
  * Hardware H264 works on the Pi 4 and Pi 400. Encoder input buffers are
    allocated on the vc4 node so the codec can import them; v3d buffers are
    scatter-gather and it cannot. An encoder that fails after construction
    falls back to libx264 instead of erroring out with an empty file, and
    the encoder drops the DRM master its vc4 open implies, so a panel or
    offscreen render coexists with a KMS render in either launch order.
  * One render loop: -o, --display and --h264 are a list of sinks a single
    render feeds, and --serve attaches the console to any of them. The
    console can drive SPI and I2C panels, not only KMS.
  * --display-opts passes driver options from the CLI: geometry, offsets,
    pins, bus speed, madctl. ghee displays lists each driver's options.
  * GET /frame.png returns one lossless PNG of the running scene; 409 while
    the scene has a compile error, 503 on a dead loop.
  * /stats reworked: one fps definition, frame_ms, stream_fps, an out list
    naming every destination frames reach, and a stale flag when the scene's
    files changed on disk; the console offers the reload. /scene for the
    active scene answers with the running document, not the file.
  * Stream viewers ping; a stream whose viewer stopped answering is dropped.
  * A scene-level common block is shared by every pass; filters never
    receive it. Scene arguments are declared per scene and listed by
    `ghee render <scene> -- --help`; scene-facing environment variables are
    gone. Bundled examples resolve only behind --demo.
  * A DT uniform carries the real frame period to every pass.
  * _sample and _sample2 interpolate identically on every GPU. On V3D this
    replaces silently-nearest sampling of float textures with the correct
    lerp, at about 1 ms per call per 1080p frame; other platforms keep
    hardware filtering at no cost.
  * 8-bit data textures upload with unpack alignment 1, fixing sheared 2D
    inputs of odd width.
  * A page flip a slow board has not finished is waited for instead of
    being treated as stuck.
  * ghee --version reports the running code; the version is single-sourced
    from ghee/__init__.py.

 -- holofermes <1163915+holofermes@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:30:00 -0400

ghee (0.2.0) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * ISF import: Interactive Shader Format shaders convert to ghee scenes or
    filters, from a file or a URL.
  * Shared console core, so an embedding host and the standalone server
    behave the same. Engine and packaging fixes.
  * ffmpeg moves from Recommends to Suggests: only boards without the
    Broadcom encoder need it, so apt no longer pulls it in.
  * CLI failures print one line instead of a traceback. GHEE_TRACEBACK=1
    brings the stack back.
  * A C engine that fails to build now fails the install, instead of
    shipping a package that cannot render. GHEE_LIB renders with an engine
    already on the host; GHEE_SKIP_ENGINE=1 installs the Python side alone.

 -- holofermes <1163915+holofermes@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 11:50:09 -0400

